      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I guess the feature request is that the heads up elements be allocated a layer separate from the regular UI layer? \n\nI think one issue in the background is that the use of the layers needs to be coordinated between worlds and VRChat UI, possibly enforced via \"gentleman's agreement\" and ToS rather than technical means. \n\nI did see a meme world where there is an nft on display, a commonly depicted one, and the joke was that it wouldn't show up in photos.\n\nSo to actually focus on the feature request, I saw an issue mentioning that reserved2 needs to be renamed in the SDK\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/internalui19-layer-is-still-listed-as-reserved2-in-the-world-sdk\n\nI didn't look at how many layers there are or how many are in use by VRChat and such.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-19T18:10:06.680Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am not sure if I like that, sometimes I take pictures with the UI layer turned on to either take pictures with visible name tags or to take pictures of UI elements that the world creator forgot to set on the default layer.\n\nThe issue is that the UI layer also takes a picture of the microphone icon and the face mirror, and that can be pretty annoying, example picture bellow.",
